 AgentAcquisition handles getting an AI agent onto the device.
 Three paths: bundled (on the .img), local (load from USB/disk),
 or network (download from a trusted source). Every path ends
 with signature verification before the agent is registered.

 The 16 GB USB stick carries everything: OS, compiler, source,
 and optionally a pre-bundled agent model. First boot detects
 whether an agent is present and offers to set the agent up.

 We say:

Section: Acquisition Method

  AcquisitionMethod =
    | AcquireBundled
    | AcquireLocal (Text)
    | AcquireNetwork (Text)

  acquisition-label : AcquisitionMethod -> Text
  acquisition-label (m) = when m
    is AcquireBundled -> "bundled (on boot image)"
    is AcquireLocal (path) -> "local: " & path
    is AcquireNetwork (url) -> "network: " & url

Section: Agent Package

 An agent package is a directory containing a manifest (name,
 version, author key, model spec), the GGUF model weights, the
 agent CDX binary (signed), and the tokenizer vocabulary.

  AgentPackage = record {
    manifest : AgentManifest,
    model-path : Text,
    cdx-path : Text,
    vocab-path : Text,
    model-spec : ModelSpec,
    verified : Boolean
  }

  PackageValidation =
    | PackageValid (AgentPackage)
    | PackageInvalid (Text)

Section: Bundled Agent Discovery

  BundledAgentResult =
    | BundledFound (Text)
    | BundledNone

  discover-bundled-agent : Text -> [FileSystem.Read, Device.Block] BundledAgentResult
  discover-bundled-agent (image-root) =
    let agent-dir = image-root & "/agent"
    in let manifest-path = agent-dir & "/manifest.json"
    in if file-exists manifest-path then BundledFound agent-dir
    else BundledNone

Section: Package Verification

  verify-agent-package : AgentPackage, Keyring, TrustLattice -> [FileSystem.Read, Device.Block] PackageValidation
  verify-agent-package (pkg) (kr) (lat) =
    if file-exists (pkg.cdx-path) == False then PackageInvalid "agent.cdx not found"
    else if file-exists (pkg.model-path) == False then PackageInvalid "model.gguf not found"
    else if pkg.verified == False then PackageInvalid "package not verified"
    else PackageValid pkg

Section: Acquisition Menu

  acquisition-menu : BundledAgentResult -> MenuState
  acquisition-menu (bundled) =
    menu-new "Agent Setup" [
      when bundled
        is BundledFound (path) -> menu-item ("Use Bundled Agent (" & path & ")") "bundled"
        is BundledNone -> menu-item-disabled "No Bundled Agent" "bundled",
      menu-item "Load from USB Drive" "usb",
      menu-item "Load from Disk Path" "local",
      menu-item "Download from Network" "network",
      menu-item "Skip (no agent)" "skip",
      menu-item "Back" "back"
    ]

Section: Agent Sizing Guide

 Model size estimates for the 16 GB stick budget.
 OS plus compiler plus source plus tests takes about 10 MB.
 Agent CDX plus vocab takes about 2 MB.
 Model weights get the remaining 15+ GB.
 TinyLlama Q4 at 600 MB fits easily for code assist.
 CodeLlama 7B Q4 at 3800 MB fits for strong code generation.
 Mixtral 8x7B Q4 at 26 GB does not fit on a 16 GB stick.

  AgentSizeClass =
    | SizeTiny
    | SizeSmall
    | SizeMedium
    | SizeLarge

  size-class-label : AgentSizeClass -> Text
  size-class-label (s) = when s
    is SizeTiny -> "tiny (<1 GB)"
    is SizeSmall -> "small (1-2 GB)"
    is SizeMedium -> "medium (3-5 GB)"
    is SizeLarge -> "large (5+ GB)"

  recommend-size-class : Integer -> AgentSizeClass
  recommend-size-class (available-mb) =
    if available-mb >= 5000 then SizeLarge
    else if available-mb >= 3000 then SizeMedium
    else if available-mb >= 1000 then SizeSmall
    else SizeTiny

